From 359750da0e2a8f6c28a1ccf65986d65ecf8402a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:41:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] perf(app): make the release AOT-compilable and cut
 per-transition work

Android installs debuggable APKs with the 'verify' dexopt filter and never
AOT-compiles them, so every settings animation ran on JIT-compiled code (the
pulled package reported [status=run-from-apk]). Release builds are now
non-debuggable, which lets ART apply speed-profile/speed dexopt.

Alongside that:
* remember the dynamic ColorScheme, Shapes and MotionScheme in FcitxSettingsTheme
  instead of rebuilding them on every recomposition;
* parse RawConfig descriptor trees on Dispatchers.Default (they used to be parsed
  on the main thread while the page-enter animation was running);
* give AnimatedContent a null sizeTransform (both pages are full-screen, so the
  default size animation only cost per-frame measure/clip);
* mark the home row models @Immutable and remember their click lambdas so rows
  skip recomposition;
* throttle TypingStatsManager.refresh() on home re-entry (refreshIfStale) to drop
  a Room round-trip per back navigation.

Data recovery after a bad deployment now uses Settings -> Advanced -> Classic
advanced settings (export/import, auto backup) instead of 'adb run-as'.
